      },
      {
        "text": "This articulation agreement outlines the preparatory courses required in the major, based on quarter credit hours. National University courses are listed on the left, with their approved (articulated) transfer equivalents on the right. General education and campus requirements for all bachelor’s degrees are detailed in separate agreements, which can be accessed in ASSIST by selecting “General Education/Breadth” on the left panel.  Additionally, NU accepts CSU GE Breadth, IGETC, and Cal-GETC certification to fulfill its GE requirements, except for at least one upper-division GE elective. \n\nNU allows a maximum of 12 semester units (18 quarter units) of vocational/technical coursework. Transfer courses noted with \"Limits Apply to Non-CSU Transferable Courses\" will count toward this limit.\n\nFor more information on this and all degrees at National University, see Program Finder.\n \nChanges to this Agreement\nMajor requirements are subject to change. Newly articulated courses are added on a rolling basis, and the articulation status of some courses may be revised or discontinued. For the most current information, please visit ASSIST every quarter and regularly consult with an academic counselor at NU or your institution.",
